In summary, avoid using `std::rand()` in general (check out [this blog](https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/61587) for more info), and avoid directly using values from `mt19937`.
The following options should be safe:
- Using `mt19937` with `uniform_int_distribution`, where the range provided is **not** in the form of [0, 2^n)$.
- Using [splitmix64](https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Pseudo-random_numbers/Splitmix64) or a similar random number generator.

